feat(map): real wind arrows — SDF symbol layer w/ speed tint + bearing rotation

Replaces the lat/lng-based shaft+head polygons (which collapsed to invisible
sub-pixel geometry at city zoom levels) with a proper screen-space MapLibre
symbol layer:

- One Point feature per station (instead of three: tail+shaft+head)
- Shared SDF arrow icon rasterized from <canvas>, registered once on map load
- icon-rotate set per-feature to the wind bearing (met "from" + 180 deg)
- icon-color tints each arrow with its Beaufort-style speed color
- icon-size interpolated by BOTH zoom and wind speed — a 25 mph reading
  visually dominates a 5 mph one at the same zoom
- Dead-calm / direction-less stations still render as a small colored dot
- Icon re-registers on styledata so basemap swaps don't wipe it

Net result: 129 PWS readings on the SLC viewport now read as a real wind
field instead of an undifferentiated dot cluster.
